    "updated_at": "2022-04-10T11:09:42Z",
    "body": "> Please run `starship explain` to ensure this is the aws module.\r\n\r\nThis revealed that it was the gcloud module settings that showed up in the prompt. Thanks! I had experimented with disabling aws and it actually disabled part of the stuff I saw in the prompt. Guess that explains that part, since GCP isn't set up on the new machine.\r\n\r\nHowever, the start of my prompt still says `jschuur in ~` on the old machine and the new machine also didn't need me to explicitly exclude AWS or GCP to not have it show up. Could I have somehow modified some default settings elsewhere?\r\n\r\nFull `starship print-config` and `starship explain` output [here](https://gist.github.com/jschuur/c0e3ca5edf3ef0cfa055f308ab10907a), after I explicitly disabled aws and gcloud on the old machine, but not the new one. I don't know why, given the [username](https://gist.github.com/jschuur/c0e3ca5edf3ef0cfa055f308ab10907a#file-new_machine-toml-L796) setup, the prompt actually shows up as `~`.",
